{"input": "Please describe the semantic specification", "answers": ["The semantic specification, on the other hand, is split into three levels: \"scenario\" is a list of schemas and bindings between them, which describes the current event in terms of Source-Path-Goal, Container, etc.; \"referent\" is about the entities in the discourse and includes grammatical information and pointers to the ontology; \"discourse segment\" comprises utterance-specific things."], "length": 24579, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The semantic specification is a sheet that contains a lot of justification and comments on the construction formalism. It has two sides: one with a revised semantic specification and the other with a revised construction formalism. The formalism is described as a top block with a list of kinds of things that can be had, and a block with constituents. The formalism is also described as a pair that includes a designated head and a semantic head. The formalism is not fully specified and will likely change."}
